// Linux x86-64 candidate native taint validation, private unindexed arena.
// RAX=source offset, R8=mode: 0 validate_int, 1 validate_ident,
// 2 escape_c, 3 taint (trusted -> tainted copy). R12/R13/R14=live arena.
// Membership guard, exact source tag, all ready and canonical byte values
// validated before any publication. Sources up to 4096 bytes. Scratch
// 4160 bytes plus call returns. Mode 0 returns optional int (tag 1021),
// mode 1 optional string (1023); invalid syntax/overflow -> absent, not trap.
// Ident syntax ASCII letter/underscore followed by ASCII alnum/underscore,
// 1..255 bytes. Mode 2 escapes quotes, backslashes, question marks and
// nonprintable bytes exactly as transitional cap_escape_c, output <=4096.
// Mode 3 copies without modifying source tag. Modes 0..2 require tainted
// tag 2045; mode 3 requires trusted tag 4096. RAX=result offset, RDX=status.
// Capacity rejection, malformed object or mode -> no arena/cursor writes.
// All allocation extents preflighted, including identifier+option combined.
// RBX/RBP/R12/R14/R15 preserved; R13 publishes committed cursor last.
// Trusted exclusive process-lifetime arena and valid stack; no indexed
// mixing, source opcode, full taint type system or canonical ABI claim.
import "ccam_aggregate_native_record_boundary.cap";

